course: dictionary
lesson: 5638
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look and sound the same but mean different things. Ling is one of them. To find out which meaning is meant, read the words around it, which is its context. «Picture Ling drawing a horse whose legs look wrong» uses Ling as a person's name, because she is drawing and checking a photo.
explain: In nature writing, ling means a plant: «ling heather» covers the moors. In a fish shop, ling is a fish, and the clue is the word fillet. Look for the clue words around ling, then swap in your meaning to check that it fits.
explain: Ling can also be a Chinese sound. «líng» means zero in Mandarin, and it is not an English word. It helps to know that the same spelling can hide several meanings, and that the sentence tells you which one to choose.
fact: Ling has several meanings: a fish, a plant, a Chinese sound and a name.
fact: As a fish, ling is a long sea fish of the cod family, caught for food.
fact: As a plant, ling is heather, a low shrub with small purple flowers that grows on moors.
fact: In Mandarin, «líng» means zero, as in líng bǐ sān, which means nil-three.
fact: A reference is a photo or object you look at while you draw, like the photo Ling checked for her horse.
exercise: «Picture Ling drawing a horse whose legs look wrong.» In this sentence, what is Ling? | *A person's name | A fish | A plant on the moor | A word meaning zero
exercise: Mum buys ling at the fish shop for tea. What does ling mean here? | A person's name | Purple flowers on the moor | Zero | *A long sea fish
exercise: The hills were covered in ling, with small purple flowers. What is ling here? | A Chinese number | *A low shrub, a kind of heather | A horse | A fish
test: «A reference is a photo or object you look at while you draw.» What is a reference? | A kind of heather | *A photo or object you look at while you draw | A fish from the North Atlantic | The name of a horse
test: Li says «líng bǐ sān» at the game. What does líng mean in it? | Ling, the name | Heather | *Zero | A fish
exam: In «Ling checked the photo for her horse», what is ling? | Zero in Mandarin | A long sea fish | *A person's name | A plant on the moor
